{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "model": "openai/gpt-5.6-sol",
  "instructions": [
    "__OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR__/opencode.local.instructions.md"
  ],
  "agent": {
    "compaction": {
      "model": "openai/gpt-5.6-sol",
      "variant": "xhigh",
      "prompt": "Create a compact but complete continuation summary for a fresh session. Start with `Original User Goal` derived from root user messages and `Goal Status`, then preserve constraints, decisions, worktree state, changed files, validation evidence, failures, risks, todos, lifecycle state, and exact next action. Do not call tools or continue the task. End with `Session Reflection`: Outcome; Slowest Loop Or Largest Time Sink; Concrete Evidence; Likely Cause And Uncertainty; Do Not Repeat. Assess stagnation: it exists when at least two materially similar cheap/local attempts since the last observable progress produced no new accepted artifact, decision-changing evidence, resolved blocker outside the same still-failing chain, or downstream boundary advancement. A new exception, log, failing line, or later failure in the same runner/evaluator chain is diagnosis, not outcome progress, and does not reset stagnation. Changed flags, wording, timeout, prompt details, retry count, or the first failing line remain the same strategy unless the causal mechanism changed. Classify `Live-Attempt Gate: clear | blocked | unknown`. One evidence-only failure after an external, physical, costly, destructive, or long-running attempt makes the gate blocked; missing gate evidence is unknown, never inferred clear, and unknown blocks another high-cost live attempt. For blocked or unknown emit `Failure Chain`, `Preserved Raw Bundles`, `Offline Replay Coverage`, `Terminal Replay Result`, and `Unlock Condition`. The gate clears only when the candidate post-run/evaluator chain has replayed preserved bundles without live effects through its terminal verdict and every downstream stage reachable for the actual run mode, including non-side-effecting finalization checks, or when the exact missing raw observation is identified. Fixing only the first failing line, helper, or parser is insufficient. If a missing observation requires live capture, classify the next attempt as bounded evidence capture rather than proof. When stagnation exists and its attempts are not yet persisted, emit `Pending Strategy History` entries containing objective, approach, evidence, outcome, reason, do-not-repeat condition, and evidence-based retry condition. Compaction cannot write files; the next session must append pending entries to `openspec/changes/<change>/history.md` before substantial work, read existing history, and must not repeat a strategy without new evidence satisfying its retry condition. For stagnation or a blocked/unknown live-attempt gate, emit exactly one materially different gate-closing `Next Strategy`. Then emit one compact `Improvement Matrix` with rows `Quality`, `Cycle Speed`, and `Token Economy`, and columns `Working Repository` and `opencode-kit`. Every cell must contain `evidence -> smallest cheap improvement -> expected benefit -> cost/risk`, or `none` when this session supplies no evidence. Admit only local, reversible, low-cost candidates with a direct causal link to the next user-visible result and no scope expansion. Matrix entries are candidates, not selected actions. End with `Next-Session Action: <exactly one Working Repository improvement or none>`; never select a list or one action per direction. For a blocked/unknown gate, this final action and `Next Strategy` must name the same first gate-closing offline step; a matrix item cannot preempt it and another high-cost live attempt is prohibited. Otherwise select only one highest-ROI goal-linked improvement and then continue the accepted outcome. Use `unknown` for unobserved timing, cause, or gate state. Keep kit candidates visible but never select a non-blocking kit item while unrelated project work is incomplete unless the owner included kit work. If the goal is missing, ambiguous, or conflicting, call `session_delivery_context` once when available rather than launch a reviewer. Deterministic code may enforce explicit structure, inventory, privacy, or mirror facts but must not score instruction effectiveness; use a dedicated same-model baseline-versus-candidate workflow with observable quality oracles for behavior changes."
    }
  },
  "plugin": [
    "opencode-pty"
  ],
  "mcp": {
    "serena": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": [
        "serena",
        "start-mcp-server",
        "--context",
        "ide",
        "--project-from-cwd"
      ],
      "cwd": ".",
      "enabled": true,
      "timeout": 60000
    },
    "codebase-memory-mcp": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": [
        "codebase-memory-mcp"
      ],
      "cwd": ".",
      "enabled": true,
      "timeout": 60000
    }
  },
  "experimental": {
    "batch_tool": true
  },
  "tool_output": {
    "max_lines": 800,
    "max_bytes": 30000
  },
  "compaction": {
    "auto": true,
    "reserved": 12000,
    "tail_turns": 2,
    "preserve_recent_tokens": 12000
  },
  "watcher": {
    "ignore": [
      "**/.git/**",
      "**/node_modules/**",
      "**/dist/**",
      "**/build/**",
      "**/coverage/**",
      "**/.next/**",
      "**/target/**"
    ]
  },
  "permission": "allow"
}
